      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T00:49:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You might want to simply call `log::fatal()` here with an appropriate message.\nI am not sure that marking the controller as broken will change anything...\n\n```\nlog::fatal(\"HCI command timeout!\");\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 284,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "c2627e7ba412378ae2e48b95cb3dcbe7e914e7eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20c6d660_a424b66d",
        "filename": "system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T03:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intention was to terminate the process but not crash. Marking the controller broken is one of the method defined in Floss Hal to stop reading and sending packets to the controller. The reason why we don\u0027t want to crash is because ChromeOS takes crash rate seriously and there are some models that using old firmware which are unlikely to get more support from vendor and hit this crash in some random situation. We understand that Android has different policy so I wonder if we can use a sysprop to separate them.",
      "parentUuid": "98a22c00_580a2957",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 284,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "c2627e7ba412378ae2e48b95cb3dcbe7e914e7eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8357a73c_cc69cac2",
        "filename": "system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T15:27:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is an appropriate use of a system property here, I would rather have the behavior be different on Floss the way you are doing here.\n\nYou say that this timeout is being triggered, I consider that to be worthy of a crash report to be honest, except if there is a likely explanation for it.\n\nCan you share more about the context for the reported HCI timeouts ?",
      "parentUuid": "20c6d660_a424b66d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 284,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "c2627e7ba412378ae2e48b95cb3dcbe7e914e7eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
